course: dictionary
lesson: 7409
title: Pointless: no purpose
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Pointless means having no purpose or use. If something is pointless, it will not help or change anything. People say «It's pointless» when trying again will not make a difference.
explain: Look at the words around it for clues. «Walking away from a pointless argument can be calm and strong, not weak.» An argument that goes round in circles and solves nothing is pointless, so walking away is sensible. Ask: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence.
explain: In games and tests, pointless has a second meaning: a team that scores no points is pointless. The words around it will show you which meaning is used. Look for clues like points, scores or games.
fact: Pointless means having no purpose or use.
fact: «Pointless» can also mean scoring no points in a game or test.
fact: Useful phrases: it's pointless to …, a pointless argument, completely pointless.
fact: «Pointlessly» means in a way that has no purpose.
fact: «Pointlessness» means the state of having no purpose or use.
exercise: «Walking away from a pointless argument can be calm and strong, not weak.» What does pointless mean here? | *An argument that solves nothing | An argument that is very loud | An argument about points in a game | A fun argument with friends
exercise: Tom says, «Our team is pointless, we have zero points.» What does pointless mean in a game? | Playing with a ball | *Scoring no points | Having a great plan | Feeling very tired
exercise: «Reading-log comments are meant to show what you thought, so copied ones are pointless.» Why are copied comments pointless? | They are in the wrong book | They are too short to read | They are written in pencil | *They do not show what you really thought
test: Lily says, «It's pointless to keep arguing with him.» What does pointless suggest? | Arguing makes him happy | *Arguing will not change anything | Arguing is great fun | Arguing will win him over
test: «Philosophy is not pointless: science and many school subjects began as philosophy.» What does this sentence say about philosophy? | It is a game with points | *It has a real purpose and helped lead to science | It is only for adults | It has no use at all
exam: «Dares often come with a false choice, but there are other reasons to say no: it's just pointless.» What does pointless mean here? | It is very exciting and worth trying | *Doing it would have no purpose, so you can say no | It will score you extra points | It must be done straight away
